## How to Manually Hunt on This Tech Stack
Since automated scanners cannot find business logic or deep application flaws, you should pivot to testing the live pages you discovered in pages.csv:
## 1. Test for SQL Injection (SQLi) on Categories/Posts
The URLs you found look like this: https://1w.run/blog/categories/1winpromo.

* What to look for: The word 1winpromo or ed is a parameter being sent to the backend database to fetch specific posts.
* How to test: Using your web browser or Burp Suite, try appending common database characters to the end of the URL path (e.g., 1winpromo' or 1winpromo") to see if the page breaks gracefully or prints a raw database query error.

## 2. Test for Broken Authentication on the Partner Sign-Up Form
Navigate manually to the main login or registration page of the affiliate portal.

* What to look for: Look closely at how the application registers a new partner account.
* How to test: Open your browser's Developer Tools (F12) and watch the Network tab when you hit submit. Check if the frontend sends extra fields (like role or is_admin) that you can manipulate to gain unauthorized access privileges.

